WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.677
"What do you mean, the trolls got Gliss?" Perda exclaimed.

2
00:00:03.678 --> 00:00:08.439
Darb was breathing hard; he'd obviously run the whole way to the meeting spot.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.310
"We landed by the riverbank, just like Zann told us to," he said.

4
00:00:13.311 --> 00:00:15.756
"At first we thought we were okay.

5
00:00:15.757 --> 00:00:21.177
Then some trolls appeared out of nowhere and grabbed Gliss before we realized they were even there.

6
00:00:21.178 --> 00:00:26.216
I tried to stop them, but they pushed me down and carried her away."

7
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:29.948
Zann was too stunned to speak for a moment.

8
00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:33.211
"This is all my fault," he blurted out at last.

9
00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:37.169
"I told Gliss she'd be safe, and she believed me."

10
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.016
"It's not your fault, Zann," Perda said.

11
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.454
"We all knew we were taking a risk."

12
00:00:42.455 --> 00:00:45.255
"We need to rescue her," Zann said.

13
00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:49.577
"We have to go to the zoo and find the wild dragon pen."

14
00:00:49.578 --> 00:00:53.787
Perda shook her head. "Sounds like a great way to get all of us captured.

15
00:00:53.788 --> 00:00:58.571
We need to stick to our plan and find the Magic Masters you've been telling us about.

16
00:00:58.572 --> 00:01:02.221
They might have some ideas about how to rescue Gliss."

17
00:01:02.222 --> 00:01:05.078
For a second Zann wanted to argue.

18
00:01:05.079 --> 00:01:09.970
He knew that Gliss must be terrified, and he wanted to rescue her if he could.

19
00:01:09.971 --> 00:01:12.532
But he also knew that Perda was right.

20
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:16.719
Rushing to the zoo would only get them all captured. They needed help.

21
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:24.292
"Okay," he said. "One of Boz's friends lives really close to here. Let's try him first. Follow me."

22
00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:27.793
Zann led his friends to a house a few blocks away.

23
00:01:27.794 --> 00:01:30.821
When he knocked, a young woman opened the door.

24
00:01:30.822 --> 00:01:34.034
Her eyes looked red, as if she'd been crying.

25
00:01:34.035 --> 00:01:38.792
"Yes?" she said, sounding suspicious. "What do you want?"

26
00:01:38.793 --> 00:01:45.014
"Uh, hello," Zann said. "We're looking for Lonz. Does he still live here?

27
00:01:45.015 --> 00:01:48.231
He's an old friend of my grandfather's, and . . ."

28
00:01:48.232 --> 00:01:51.814
His voice trailed off as the young woman started sobbing.

29
00:01:51.815 --> 00:01:56.812
She hid her face in her hands.

30
00:01:56.813 --> 00:02:05.043
"Lonz is my father. He was one of the first Reds they took!" she said, her words muffled and sad.

31
00:02:05.044 --> 00:02:08.912
Zann's heart sank. "I'm sorry," he said.

32
00:02:08.913 --> 00:02:15.166
"My grandfather was taken too. I'm really sorry."

33
00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:18.953
"Now what?" Darb asked a moment later as they walked away.

34
00:02:18.954 --> 00:02:23.019
"Do you think Morb already captured all of Boz's friends?"

35
00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.317
"I hope not," Perda said, sounding worried.

36
00:02:26.318 --> 00:02:29.010
Zann tried not to think about that possibility.

37
00:02:29.011 --> 00:02:35.721
"Boz's friend Saffa lives right across the river from here," he said. "Let's try her house next."

38
00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:39.207
They walked as quickly as they could, watching out for trolls.

39
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:44.302
Every time they saw one, they ducked into a doorway or behind a tree.

40
00:02:44.303 --> 00:02:50.250
Finally they reached a neighborhood of brightly colored homes with small but tidy front yards.

41
00:02:50.251 --> 00:02:54.206
Zann had to stop to think about which one belonged to Boz's friend.

42
00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:58.249
"I wish we could check the Directory for the address," he said.

43
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:03.709
Perda frowned. "Too risky," she said. "Just try to remember."

44
00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:08.648
"I'm pretty sure it's that one." Zann led his friends to a nearby house.

45
00:03:08.649 --> 00:03:11.897
Taking a deep breath, he knocked on the door.

46
00:03:11.898 --> 00:03:17.358
A middle-aged man answered. "Yes, can I help you?" he asked in a weary voice.

47
00:03:17.359 --> 00:03:21.872
"I'm looking for Saffa," Zann said. "Is this the right house?"

48
00:03:21.873 --> 00:03:26.869
The man's face crumpled. "Yes. But my wife isn't here anymore.

49
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.682
The trolls came for her the day before yesterday.

50
00:03:29.683 --> 00:03:33.177
Saffa tried to zap away, but she wasn't fast enough."

51
00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:38.616
"We're sorry to bother you," Perda said. "I hope she comes back soon."

52
00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:41.920
Perda, Zann, and Darb returned to the street.

53
00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:45.248
"Maybe this isn't such a good idea," Darb said.

54
00:03:45.249 --> 00:03:48.868
"You said these people are all famous Magic Masters, right?

55
00:03:48.869 --> 00:03:52.986
Morb might be keeping an eye on their houses to try to catch their friends."

56
00:03:52.987 --> 00:03:55.774
Perda gulped. "Or us."

57
00:03:55.775 --> 00:04:02.661
"Maybe," Zann said. "But we have to save Gliss, and I don't know how we can do that on our own.

58
00:04:02.662 --> 00:04:06.451
Besides we haven't tried going to Teplo's house yet.

59
00:04:06.452 --> 00:04:09.586
If anyone could hide from Morb, it's him.

60
00:04:09.587 --> 00:04:14.733
Boz always said that Teplo was the most creative magician he ever knew."

61
00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:18.070
"Really?" Perda said. "What's he like?"

62
00:04:18.071 --> 00:04:26.794
"I never met him," Zann admitted. "He was away studying the nomads on the Far Frontier the whole time I lived in First City.

63
00:04:26.795 --> 00:04:31.258
But Boz has told me all kinds of cool stories about him."

64
00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:34.136
"Okay, let's go find him," Darb said.

65
00:04:34.137 --> 00:04:38.762
Perda nodded grimly. "And let's hope Morb didn't find him first."

66
00:04:38.763 --> 00:04:43.650
Soon they reached a house that looked different from any of the other homes on the block.

67
00:04:43.651 --> 00:04:50.949
It was tall and narrow, with oddly shaped windows and a statue of a gangly bird atop the pointy roof.

68
00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:55.116
"Are you sure this is the right place?" Darb sounded dubious.

69
00:04:55.117 --> 00:04:58.719
"Yes. Boz pointed it out to me a few times."

70
00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:04.161
Taking a deep breath, Zann walked up the steep front steps to the wooden porch.

71
00:05:04.162 --> 00:05:07.393
He signaled for Perda and Darb to follow him.

72
00:05:07.394 --> 00:05:11.317
Zann hoped the porch might hide them if any trolls wandered by.

73
00:05:11.318 --> 00:05:16.766
He knocked on the door. A young woman with black hair and an intelligent expression answered.

74
00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:21.662
"Hi," Zann said. "We're looking for Teplo. Is he here?"

75
00:05:21.663 --> 00:05:23.288
The young woman shook her head.

76
00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:26.928
"Sorry. He's gone, just like the rest of the Reds in town."

77
00:05:26.929 --> 00:05:29.858
The young woman closed the door in his face.

78
00:05:29.859 --> 00:05:35.377
"I can't believe Morb already captured all the Magic Masters," Perda exclaimed.

79
00:05:35.378 --> 00:05:39.285
"I can," Darb replied. "He captured Boz, didn't he?"

80
00:05:39.286 --> 00:05:42.456
Zann shrugged, opening his mouth to answer.

81
00:05:42.457 --> 00:05:47.432
But before he could say a word, he felt the porch floor shudder beneath his feet.

82
00:05:47.433 --> 00:05:58.113
A second later a trapdoor fell open, sending all three kids tumbling down into total darkness.

